SELENIUM MOUSE / KEYBOARD ACTIONS — HANDS-ON

This is a high-value Selenium coding section for SDET interviews. You should be able to write these without looking at notes.

298. What is the Actions class?
Interview answer

“The Actions class in Selenium is used to perform advanced user interactions such as mouse hover, right click, double click, drag and drop, and keyboard actions.”

Import:

import org.openqa.selenium.interactions.Actions;

Create object:

Actions actions = new Actions(driver);

Then you can perform actions such as:

actions.moveToElement(element).perform();
🔥 Why do we use Actions?

Normal Selenium:

element.click();

is enough for a normal click.

But for advanced interactions such as:

Mouse Hover
Right Click
Double Click
Drag & Drop
Keyboard shortcuts

we can use:

Actions
299. How do you perform Mouse Hover?

Use:

actions.moveToElement(element).perform();
Example

Suppose you have:

Products
    ↓
    Electronics
    Mobiles
    Laptops

The submenu appears after hovering over Products.

WebElement products =
        driver.findElement(By.id("products"));

Actions actions = new Actions(driver);

actions.moveToElement(products).perform();

Then:

driver.findElement(By.id("mobiles")).click();
⭐ Interview answer

“For mouse hover, I locate the target element and use Actions.moveToElement(element).perform().”

300. How do you perform Right Click?

Right click is called context click in Selenium.

Use:

actions.contextClick(element).perform();
Example
WebElement element =
        driver.findElement(By.id("file"));

Actions actions = new Actions(driver);

actions.contextClick(element).perform();

This performs:

Right Click
⭐ Important

Don't say:

actions.rightClick();

The Selenium method is:

contextClick()
301. How do you perform Double Click?

Use:

actions.doubleClick(element).perform();

Example:

WebElement file =
        driver.findElement(By.id("file"));

Actions actions = new Actions(driver);

actions.doubleClick(file).perform();
Alternative
actions.doubleClick().perform();

This double-clicks at the current mouse position.

But normally:

actions.doubleClick(element).perform();

is clearer.

302. How do you perform Drag and Drop?

There are several ways.

Method 1 — dragAndDrop()
actions.dragAndDrop(source, target).perform();

Example:

WebElement source =
        driver.findElement(By.id("source"));

WebElement target =
        driver.findElement(By.id("target"));

Actions actions = new Actions(driver);

actions.dragAndDrop(source, target).perform();
🔥 Method 2 — Click, Hold, Move, Release

Sometimes dragAndDrop() doesn't work properly with certain JavaScript-heavy applications.

Then use:

actions.clickAndHold(source)
       .moveToElement(target)
       .release()
       .perform();
Complete:
WebElement source =
        driver.findElement(By.id("source"));

WebElement target =
        driver.findElement(By.id("target"));

Actions actions = new Actions(driver);

actions.clickAndHold(source)
       .moveToElement(target)
       .release()
       .perform();
⭐ Strong Interview Answer

If interviewer asks:

“Drag and drop is not working using dragAndDrop(). What will you do?”

Say:

“I would first verify the source and target locators and whether the target is visible and interactable. If the normal dragAndDrop() action doesn't work because of the application's implementation, I can perform the interaction manually using clickAndHold(), moveToElement(), and release().”

Then write:

actions.clickAndHold(source)
       .moveToElement(target)
       .release()
       .perform();
303. How do you perform Keyboard Actions?

The Actions class can also simulate keyboard operations.

Examples:

actions.sendKeys(Keys.ENTER).perform();
actions.sendKeys(Keys.TAB).perform();
actions.sendKeys(Keys.ESCAPE).perform();

Import:

import org.openqa.selenium.Keys;
🔥 Example — Press ENTER
Actions actions = new Actions(driver);

actions.sendKeys(Keys.ENTER).perform();
🔥 Example — Press TAB
actions.sendKeys(Keys.TAB).perform();
🔥 Example — Escape
actions.sendKeys(Keys.ESCAPE).perform();
304. How do you perform CTRL+A?

Use:

actions.keyDown(Keys.CONTROL)
       .sendKeys("a")
       .keyUp(Keys.CONTROL)
       .perform();
Example
WebElement textbox =
        driver.findElement(By.id("username"));

textbox.click();

Actions actions = new Actions(driver);

actions.keyDown(Keys.CONTROL)
       .sendKeys("a")
       .keyUp(Keys.CONTROL)
       .perform();

This performs:

CTRL + A
🔥 Simpler Approach

You can also send the key combination directly to an element:

textbox.sendKeys(Keys.CONTROL, "a");

Example:

WebElement textbox =
        driver.findElement(By.id("username"));

textbox.sendKeys(Keys.CONTROL, "a");
Interview tip

Know both approaches.

WebElement.sendKeys()

Good for element-specific keyboard input:

textbox.sendKeys(Keys.CONTROL, "a");
Actions

Good for more complex keyboard/mouse sequences:

actions.keyDown(Keys.CONTROL)
       .sendKeys("a")
       .keyUp(Keys.CONTROL)
       .perform();
305. How do you perform CTRL+C?

Use:

actions.keyDown(Keys.CONTROL)
       .sendKeys("c")
       .keyUp(Keys.CONTROL)
       .perform();

Complete example:

WebElement textbox =
        driver.findElement(By.id("username"));

textbox.click();

Actions actions = new Actions(driver);

actions.keyDown(Keys.CONTROL)
