       .perform();
⭐ Windows/Linux vs Mac

On Windows/Linux:

Keys.CONTROL

On macOS, keyboard shortcuts commonly use:

Keys.COMMAND

For your typical Selenium interview environment, Windows + Keys.CONTROL is what you'll most commonly demonstrate.

307. How do you scroll in Selenium?

There are multiple approaches.

The modern Selenium approach is often to use JavaScript or Selenium's scrolling capabilities depending on the requirement.

Using JavaScript:

JavascriptExecutor js =
        (JavascriptExecutor) driver;

js.executeScript("window.scrollBy(0,500)");

This scrolls vertically by 500 pixels.

308. What is JavascriptExecutor?
Interview answer

“JavascriptExecutor is a Selenium interface that allows us to execute JavaScript code in the browser. I use it when a browser interaction or scrolling operation is easier to perform through JavaScript.”

Import:

import org.openqa.selenium.JavascriptExecutor;

Create:

JavascriptExecutor js =
        (JavascriptExecutor) driver;

Execute:

js.executeScript("window.scrollBy(0,500)");
🔥 Why cast WebDriver to JavascriptExecutor?

Because:

JavascriptExecutor

is an interface, and the WebDriver implementation also supports that interface.

So:

JavascriptExecutor js =
        (JavascriptExecutor) driver;

gives us access to:

executeScript()
309. How do you Scroll to an Element?

This is a very common interview coding question.

Use:

js.executeScript(
    "arguments[0].scrollIntoView(true);",
    element
);
Example
WebElement element =
        driver.findElement(By.id("footer"));

JavascriptExecutor js =
        (JavascriptExecutor) driver;

js.executeScript(
    "arguments[0].scrollIntoView(true);",
    element
);

Now the element is brought into the viewport.

🔥 What is arguments[0]?

This is worth knowing.

In:

js.executeScript(
    "arguments[0].scrollIntoView(true);",
    element
);

the JavaScript:

arguments[0]

refers to the first argument passed to executeScript().

Here:

element

is that first argument.

So:

arguments[0] → element
310. How do you Scroll to Bottom?

Use:

js.executeScript(
    "window.scrollTo(0, document.body.scrollHeight);"
);
Complete:
JavascriptExecutor js =
        (JavascriptExecutor) driver;

js.executeScript(
    "window.scrollTo(0, document.body.scrollHeight);"
);

This moves the page to the bottom.

🔥 Scroll to Top

The interviewer may immediately ask this.

js.executeScript(
    "window.scrollTo(0, 0);"
);
🔥 Scroll Down by Pixels
js.executeScript(
    "window.scrollBy(0,500);"
);

Scroll up:

js.executeScript(
    "window.scrollBy(0,-500);"
);

Remember:

Positive Y → down
Negative Y → up
311. How do you perform Horizontal Scrolling?

This is another useful coding question.

JavaScript:

js.executeScript(
    "window.scrollBy(500,0);"
);

Here:

X = 500
Y = 0

So the page moves horizontally.

🔥 Horizontal Scroll to a Specific Element

You can also use:

js.executeScript(
    "arguments[0].scrollIntoView(true);",
    element
);

But if you specifically need horizontal movement, you can use JavaScript such as:

js.executeScript(
    "arguments[0].scrollLeft = arguments[0].scrollWidth;",
    element
);

This is particularly useful when the scrollable container itself has horizontal overflow.

🔥 Real-Time Horizontal Table Scenario

Suppose your application has:

Employee Table
-------------------------------------------------------------→
Name | ID | Dept | Location | Salary | Bonus | Manager | ...

The table has a horizontal scrollbar.

You locate the scrollable container:

WebElement table =
        driver.findElement(By.id("tableContainer"));

Then:

JavascriptExecutor js =
        (JavascriptExecutor) driver;

js.executeScript(
    "arguments[0].scrollLeft = arguments[0].scrollWidth;",
    table
);

This moves the container horizontally toward the right.

🔥 Selenium Actions Scrolling

Modern Selenium also provides wheel actions.

For example:

Actions actions = new Actions(driver);

actions.scrollByAmount(0, 500).perform();

Scroll down:

actions.scrollByAmount(0, 500).perform();

Scroll up:

actions.scrollByAmount(0, -500).perform();
🔥 Scroll to Element Using Actions

You can also use:

actions.scrollToElement(element).perform();

Example:

WebElement element =
        driver.findElement(By.id("footer"));

Actions actions = new Actions(driver);

actions.scrollToElement(element).perform();
Interview advantage

If interviewer asks:

"Do you know any way other than JavaScript for scrolling?"

You can say:

“Yes. Selenium's Actions API provides wheel scrolling methods such as scrollByAmount() and scrollToElement().”

🔥 Actions vs JavascriptExecutor

This is a very good interview comparison.

Requirement	Approach
Normal click	element.click()
Mouse hover	Actions
Right click	Actions.contextClick()
Double click	Actions.doubleClick()
Drag & drop	Actions
Keyboard combinations	Actions
Scroll by wheel	Actions
Scroll to element	Actions.scrollToElement()
Execute browser JavaScript	JavascriptExecutor
Scroll using JS	JavascriptExecutor
🔥 Interview Question: "Why don't you always use JavaScript click?"

This is a 5-year-level interview question.

Don't say:

"JavaScript click is better."

Instead:

“I prefer the normal Selenium interaction first because it represents a real user interaction and also allows Selenium to perform its normal interactability checks. I use JavaScript when there is a genuine requirement, such as interacting with a specific DOM property or handling a case where standard Selenium interaction is not suitable after investigating the root cause.”

That's much stronger.

